              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_entries"} Related entries
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong two-valued topos
            is a topos with exactly two
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth values
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is called
            %em two-valued
            if its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-valued+object"} two-valued
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi true
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\overset{true}{\to}\Omega
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi false
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\overset{false}{\to}\Omega
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In particular, a two-valued topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                is consistent i.e.
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo ≠
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}\neq 1
            %li
              %p
                Since
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
                classifies subobjects
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\subseteq 1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi χ
                            %mi X
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\overset{\chi_X}{\to}\Omega
                whence a topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                is two-valued precisely if the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                has exactly the two subobjects
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %li
              %p
                Two-valued toposes are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topos"} connected
                i.e.
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≠
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\neq 1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi V
                      %mo ≅
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\coprod V\cong 1
                implies
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ≅
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\cong 1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ≅
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\cong 0
                or vice versa. This holds because
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                are disjoint subobjects of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mi V
                      %mo ≅
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\coprod V\cong 1
                but
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                has only the two trivial subobjects.
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕋
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
                be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theory"} geometric theory
                over the signature
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕋
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
                is called
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+theory"} complete
                if every geometric sentence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                is
                = succeed "-provably" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝕋
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \top
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊥
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bottom\; ,
                but not both. A geometric theory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝕋
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
                is complete precisely iff its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi 𝕋
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set[\mathbb{T}]
                is two-valued (Caramello
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#Ca12"} 2012
            %li
              %p
                Being two-valued is different from saying that
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo ≅
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega\cong 1\coprod 1
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} Boolean toposes
                but a Boolean topos is not necessarily two-valued - the easiest consistent example possibly being
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set\times Set
                which is four-valued, more complicated ones often arising in intermediates steps in set-theoretic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forcing"} forcing
                (cf.
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuum+hypothesis"} continuum hypothesis
                %em filter quotient construction
                turning a Boolean topos into a two-valued Boolean topos (cf. Mac Lane-Moerdijk
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#MM94"} 1994
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Though the forcing models resulting from the above mentioned filter-quotient construction provide a plethora of examples of Boolean two-valued toposes other than
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %li
              %p
                In fact, there exists a rich supply of two-valued toposes that are not Boolean provided by the
                %strong toposes of actions of monoids
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
                consists of all right ideals of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\in M
                acting on a right ideal
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                by mapping it to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi m
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi m
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I\cdot m=\{x\in M|m\cdot x\in I\}\;,
                a global element picks out a right ideal
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                that satisfies
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi y
                      %mo =
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J\cdot y= J
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\in M
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                with underlying set a singleton, which implies
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo =
                      %mi ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J=\empty
                or
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                        %mo =
                        %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J=M
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\in J
                entails
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi J
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mi J
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\in J\cdot j=J\;.
                Whence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi M
                            %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{M^{op}}
                is two-valued but it is a well known exercise that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi M
                            %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{M^{op}}
                is Boolean precisely iff
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                is a group.
            %li
              %p
                More generally, a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
                on a category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is two-valued if and only if C is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+graph"} strongly connected
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homset"} homset
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is inhabited (Caramello
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#Ca16"} 2016
